+  with grep of `ref(` over `dbt_project/models`.
+  what changes in the numbers: a rate goes to NULL ("—") where an input of its formula is absent
+  from a non-awarded game of its window. Measured on prod on 2026-09-18 before the change — form
+  window, 9,386 windows: `shots_on_goal_pct` shown with uncovered inputs in 138 windows (the 14
+  above 100% among them), `corners_per_match` 71, the seven player-derived rates in 1,212 of 9,116
+  windows; season surface, 13,752 team-seasons at the latest row: `shots_inside_box_pct` 84,
+  `passes_per_match` / `passes_accuracy_pct` 86, `corners_per_match` 26, the seven player-derived
+  rates 1,514 of 6,433. Downstream: the `duels_per_match` team leaderboard loses teams with
+  partial player coverage (the UNPIVOT drops NULLs); the competition benchmarks' percentiles for
+  the seven player-derived metrics span fewer teams. No column is added to or removed from any
+  mart; one coverage count per input is added to the two intermediate builders' projections —
+  shots inside the box, passes total, passes accurate, corners, and on the season record
+  opponent shots (`int_team_season__metrics_cumulative` reads them without projecting, so
+  `int_team_season__metrics`' shape and `assert_no_uncatalogued_season_metric` are untouched).
+  what imports it: `assert_mart_team_season_insights_metric_consistency` (shots_per_match ×
+  games_with_team_stats — unchanged), `assert_awarded_matches_do_not_null_team_stats` and
